`verilator_config
// Each waiver names one signal and the reason it is intended. Nothing else is
// waived: tools/lint/lint.sh runs verilator --lint-only -Wall and fails on
// any other warning.
//
// SYNCASYNCNET on the OpenFrame chip's tile reset. hydra_mom_pins samples its
// personality strap (ui_in[7:4] == 4'hA) synchronously WHILE rst_n is low,
// and the same rst_n is the asynchronous input of its reset synchroniser.
// Sampling the strap from the synchronised reset instead would extend the
// window two clocks past the release, when ui_in[7:4] is already the legacy
// completion tag, so the strap could be misread. The Tiny Tapeout tile has
// no strap and needs no waiver.
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET -file "*" -match "*tile_rst_n*"
